WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:02.400
Tea tree oil is touted

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:04.500
as having anti-
fungal properties.

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:07.560
So what happens when
it’s put to the test

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:09.480
against a variety of
fungal infections?

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:12.060
Watch the video
to find out.

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:18.334
"Does Tea Tree Oil Work for Dandruff,
Athlete’s Foot and Nail Fungus?"

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:21.360
Our entire understanding
of the cause of dandruff

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:25.260
shifted with this landmark
article published in 1984.

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:29.940
Instead of relying on secondary sources,
reviews, editorials, opinion pieces,

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:33.180
he looked at the primary literature,
the original studies,

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:37.860
and was amazed to find out how
overwhelming was the evidence

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:41.100
of the true cause, and
how it had been ignored,

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:44.640
because it was so well buried
under the mountain of error,

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:48.600
since some expert in the 1800s
put forth some bogus theory.

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:52.200
We now know that dandruff
is triggered by a fungus

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.780
that lives and feeds
on the human scalp,

00:00:54.780 --> 00:01:00.240
the two major implications being: first,
how alarming it is that some bogus theory

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:03.960
can remain in the medical literature
unchallenged for a century

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:05.880
despite evidence to the contrary;

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:11.220
and second, hey, if it's a fungus,
what about trying tea tree oil,

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:14.040
which contains components
that have anti-fungal activity

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.420
against a range of fungi.

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:18.120
That was based on
studies like this, though,

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:22.260
where tea tree oil in a Petri dish
can fight off pathogenic skin fungi.

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:26.760
But you don't know if it works for
dandruff until you put it to the test.

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:30.060
A hundred and twenty-six men and
women randomized to daily use

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:33.420
of a 5% tea tree oil shampoo
or placebo for a month.

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:36.180
The placebo worked a little bit,

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:38.400
decreasing dandruff
severity by about 10%,

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:43.140
but the tea tree oil shampoo
worked better, about a 40% drop.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:47.760
Looks like more than
40% from the graph,

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:52.560
but that's because they misleadingly
started the Y-axis at negative 60.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:58.260
This is a classic deception featured
in chapter 5 of the 1954 classic,

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:00.300
"How to Lie with Statistics."

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:06.060
The graph should really look like this,
which makes the effect less impressive,

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:08.100
but it was still
statistically significant.

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:13.320
Only one patient in the tea tree oil group
actually achieved a complete response,

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:16.020
though one in the
placebo group did as well.

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:20.220
Thus, it seems that tea tree oil shampoo
would require ongoing application

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:21.780
for control of dandruff.

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:26.760
Speaking of fungus, what about tea tree
oil in the treatment of athlete's foot?

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:30.420
That may actually be our most
common fungal skin infection,

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:32.340
affecting up to 1 in 10.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:35.880
So, about a hundred patients
randomized into one of three groups:

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:42.900
a 10% tea tree oil cream, tinactin, an
antifungal drug, or a placebo cream.

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:48.120
A month later, the fungus was wiped
out in 85% of the drug group,

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:51.480
but only about a quarter of the
placebo and tea tree oil groups.

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:55.620
This is somewhat surprising, since
tea tree oil can kill off the fungus

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:59.040
in a Petri dish, but
apparently not on toes.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:03.480
That reminds me of some of the
oral health data on tea tree oil.

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:07.080
It can wipe out some oral
pathogens in a Petri dish,

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:10.260
but have people swish a tea tree oil
solution around in their mouth,

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:14.580
and here's the dental plaque buildup
after 4 days of no brushing,

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:16.200
swishing with a placebo.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:19.920
Here's swishing with a medicated
chlorhexidine mouthwash,

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:22.380
which keeps the
plaque a bit at bay.

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:25.980
But the tea tree oil mouth rinse?
No effect.

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:29.400
So, if tea tree oil doesn't influence
the amount of plaque,

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:31.680
presumably it wouldn't
help with gingivitis,

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:34.200
the gum inflammation that's
caused by plaque buildup.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:36.900
But, no, here's the twist.

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:40.800
True, no reduction in plaque
with a 2.5% tea tree oil gel.

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:45.180
Yet significant reduction
in gingivitis scores.

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:49.440
Since decreased gum inflammation
occurred without a decrease in plaque,

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:53.100
it appeared to just be helping
more from an anti-inflammatory

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:55.680
rather than
antimicrobial mechanism.

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:58.560
Might the same thing
be happening here?

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:03.360
Yeah, from a mycological cure
standpoint—a fungus cure standpoint—

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:06.780
tea tree oil didn't really do
any better than placebo.

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:10.740
But though the drug wiped out
the fungus in 85% of cases,

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:15.120
in some of those cases, the patients
actually didn't notice an improvement

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:17.940
in symptoms, or they actually
felt worse after the drug,

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:22.260
probably a reflection of
tinactin's irritant side effects.

00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:27.000
If instead of mycological cure, you
looked at symptom improvement,

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:31.260
tea tree oil works
as well as the drug.

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:35.040
So, this may be the basis for
the popular use of tea tree oil

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:36.420
in the treatment
of athlete's foot,

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:40.200
but people should realize that
it's just symptomatic relief,

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:42.960
and they're not necessarily
eliminating the underlying cause.

00:04:43.620 --> 00:04:47.040
Of course, maybe they didn't use
a strong enough concentration.

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:52.380
And indeed, if you go with not a 10%
cream, but up to 25 or 50%,

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:56.520
you can get mycological cure
rates above that of placebo,

00:04:56.520 --> 00:04:58.680
but still not as
good as the drug.

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:02.340
And at those high concentrations, some
of the patients applying tea tree oil

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:06.060
developed moderate to severe
dermatitis—they broke out in a rash.

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:07.920
But, hey, if you
have a patient

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:09.840
that doesn't want to use
the medicated creams,

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:13.380
then a 25% tea tree oil application
has a decent chance

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:15.780
of knocking it out without
being too risky.

00:05:15.780 --> 00:05:22.010
But the standard over-the-counter
antifungal creams may work better.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:26.760
Onychomycosis is a fungal
infection of our nails,

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:29.340
usually toenails, but
sometimes fingernails,

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:33.540
characterized by nail discoloration,
deformity, detachment, thickening,

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:34.920
crumbling, ridging.

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:37.320
Here’s an example of
what it can look like.

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:40.380
Reported prevalence
is estimated

00:05:40.380 --> 00:05:42.120
to be about 1
in 25 people,

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:44.940
though it’s more common
in older individuals:

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:46.440
1 in 5 over 60,

00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:49.140
and like half of
70-year-olds.

00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:51.120
Unfortunately, it’s
really hard to treat,

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:52.740
because the
fungus can hide

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:54.060
deep inside
the nail,

00:05:54.060 --> 00:05:56.280
protected from the blood
supply on one side

00:05:56.280 --> 00:05:57.960
or anything you
want to put on

00:05:57.960 --> 00:05:59.100
topically on
the other.

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:01.140
So, recurrence
after treatment

00:06:01.140 --> 00:06:04.020
is common due
to residual fungus,

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:06.060
even if you are able
to beat it back.

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:10.440
Many of the oral systemic
treatments can be toxic,

00:06:10.440 --> 00:06:12.240
and many topical
applications

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:14.220
require long
treatment courses,

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:16.200
which may limit
patient compliance,

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:17.760
especially in
patients who want

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:19.020
to use nail
polish or

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:20.100
something to
cover it up.

00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:22.260
So, given all
the problems

00:06:22.260 --> 00:06:24.960
with a lot of
prescription anti-fungals,

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:26.160
there has been
renewed interest

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:28.080
in natural remedies.

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:30.240
Well, if tea tree
oil can affect

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:32.340
athlete’s foot and
dandruff fungus,

00:06:32.340 --> 00:06:34.680
what about
nail fungus?

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:37.440
Well, there was
this study

00:06:37.440 --> 00:06:39.300
of a combination of
the antifungal drug

00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:42.120
in Lotrimin cream
with tea tree oil

00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:45.600
that seemed
pretty effective—

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:47.100
compared to nothing.

00:06:47.100 --> 00:06:49.260
But, what about compared
to each other?

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:52.980
Well, there was one
head-to-head study

00:06:52.980 --> 00:06:54.900
comparing tea tree
oil with a

00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:56.100
common antifungal drug,

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:58.680
a double-blind, randomized
controlled trial:

00:06:58.680 --> 00:07:00.540
twice-daily
application of either

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:02.880
the drug or pure
tea tree oil

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:04.560
on the nail
for 6 months.

00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:07.200
Debridement was performed
every few months,

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:08.760
where some of
the fungal mass

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:10.500
is debulked, scraped,
ground off.

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:14.760
And, after 6 months,
the drug only

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:16.560
wiped the fungus
out completely

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:18.660
in about 1 in 10 cases,

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:20.220
but looked better,
with partial

00:07:20.220 --> 00:07:22.020
or full resolution
of the appearance,

00:07:22.020 --> 00:07:23.880
in the majority of
patients either

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:26.160
from the doctor’s assessment
or the patient’s.

00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:31.200
And, the tea tree oil
did just as well.

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:33.900
The two preparations
were comparable

00:07:33.900 --> 00:07:36.300
in efficacy of cure,
clinical assessment,

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:37.620
and subjective improvement—

00:07:37.620 --> 00:07:39.960
even their cost
was comparable.

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:42.960
So, for patients desiring
a “natural” treatment for

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:44.220
athlete’s foot
or nail fungus,

00:07:44.220 --> 00:07:46.620
topical tea tree
oil is a reasonable

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:48.180
alternative to
prescription or

00:07:48.180 --> 00:07:50.040
over-the-counter
anti-fungals.

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:53.040
Speaking of natural
treatments,

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:55.560
how about a truly
natural treatment.

00:07:56.220 --> 00:07:58.320
One potential reason
for the poor

00:07:58.320 --> 00:08:00.000
long-term benefits
of any therapy

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:02.340
for nail fungus is
that it may be

00:08:02.340 --> 00:08:03.720
only treating
a manifestation

00:08:03.720 --> 00:08:05.280
of underlying disease,

00:08:05.280 --> 00:08:07.920
such as generalized
immune suppression

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:11.340
or peripheral micro- or
macrovascular disease.

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:13.620
Maybe fungal nail
infections are just

00:08:13.620 --> 00:08:15.960
a manifestation of
poor peripheral

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:18.000
blood circulation
that would normally

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:19.620
allow your body’s
natural defenses

00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:20.640
to keep the
fungus from

00:08:20.640 --> 00:08:21.780
taking root in
the first place.

00:08:22.740 --> 00:08:24.600
Evidently, there
was a non-English

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:26.100
language study
of 400 patients

00:08:26.100 --> 00:08:27.540
that looked at
the “relationship

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:29.820
between blood circulation
of the skin

00:08:29.820 --> 00:08:31.440
and the development
of fungus disease”—

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:32.940
that was the title—and

00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:35.160
“found a greater
than 50% reduction

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:36.540
in blood flow
in patients with

00:08:36.540 --> 00:08:38.100
[athlete’s foot
and nail fungus]…

00:08:38.100 --> 00:08:40.560
compared with patients
without these disorders.”

00:08:40.560 --> 00:08:42.540
So, if fungal nail
infections are

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:44.880
just a symptom of
an underlying process,

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:46.980
then treatment
aimed at eradication

00:08:46.980 --> 00:08:49.140
of a pathogen may
be unrealistic.

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:51.720
No wonder it just
grows right back.

00:08:51.720 --> 00:08:53.760
A more appropriate
goal, then,

00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:56.400
may be to just give
up and live with it.

00:08:56.400 --> 00:08:57.900
But wait!

00:08:57.900 --> 00:08:59.700
If it’s a circulation problem,

00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:02.880
why not try to instead
improve the circulation.

00:09:02.880 --> 00:09:06.300
We’ve known
since the 1950s

00:09:06.300 --> 00:09:07.680
that you can
effectively switch

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:09.540
peripheral artery
circulation on

00:09:09.540 --> 00:09:10.920
and off like
a light switch

00:09:10.920 --> 00:09:12.960
within days by
switching people

00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:14.580
between a low fat
plant-based diet

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:16.200
and the more
conventional diet

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:17.820
that contributed
to the problem

00:09:17.820 --> 00:09:20.751
in the first place.

